# URLs the link checker must not fail on, with a reason for each. An entry here
# is a check switched off, so the list stays short and justified.
#
# These are regular expressions, one per line.

# ACM's DOI host answers 403 to non-browser user agents. The DOI is stable and
# citing it is the point; it cannot be verified from CI.
dl\.acm\.org

# crates.io rate limits automated traffic and answers 429 in bursts. Crate
# existence is already proven by the build resolving the dependency.
crates\.io

# Cloudflare-fronted mirrors of the winget catalogue block datacentre IPs.
winstall\.app

# Requires an authenticated session; always 999 for anonymous requests.
linkedin\.com

# --- Temporary: delete this block once v0.1.0 is published (added 2026-07-28) ---
#
# These three cannot resolve before the first release exists, and the release
# cannot be published before the `ci` check is green. That is a deadlock, not
# link rot:
#
#  - the compare range and the tag page 404 until the v0.1.0 tag is pushed;
#  - the release workflow's badge 404s until that workflow has run at least
#    once, which only a tag can trigger.
#
# Each pattern names v0.1.0 explicitly rather than matching /compare/ or
# /releases/tag/ generally, so a genuinely broken link to a later version is
# still reported.
Yet-to-be-JoJo-s-RPG-Game-/compare/v0\.1\.0\.\.\.HEAD
Yet-to-be-JoJo-s-RPG-Game-/releases/tag/v0\.1\.0
actions/workflows/release\.yml/badge\.svg
